From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ScarlettMac <scarlettmac@local>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 16:32:06 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 11/15] shader: lane-alike branches run together; scalar inputs
 are per wave

VICTORY_WAVE_WHY=1 on ds-past3 showed the remaining first-lane refusals:
34 shaders, all a v_readfirstlane_b32 in a block in_step called not
together, whose value comes from v_cvt_u32_f32/v_floor_f32/v_mul_legacy/
buffer_load_format_x/v_cndmask_b32 or a program input. Those are loop
counts and indices computed by vector float math that is one value per
console wave.

in_step now treats a branch on a lane condition in
halves::lane_uniform as running together, like a scalar one, and
lane_uniform seeds the scalar inputs (user data, system values; not EXEC
or VCC) as one value per wave. That lets across_here/exchange_halves take
those first lanes exactly instead of refusing them, and lets barrier
placement see the loops as in step. lane_uniform is computed once and
shared by the barrier and halves paths.

Host cargo test -p victory-shader: 213 pass.
